HWINFO [ALL]
  The hardware CyborgOS can see: the expansion ROMs by name, the V9990,
  the DS12887 clock, the Net4CPC, the M4, the Albireos (ALL: with an M4
  too), the SYMBiFACE II mouse, the speech ports, the CPC Booster.
  It only reads (a V9990 register written is put back).
The hardware tests (disc 8), each claiming what it drives:
  RTCTEST [SET yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm:ss]  the DS12887's date and time (RTC)
  M4TIME                       the M4's clock (it sets it from NTP)
  NTPTEST [a.b.c.d]            the time from an NTP server over the
                               Net4CPC (W5100) - time.google.com if
                               no address is given
  SPEAK [SSA | DKT] words      allophones to an SSA-1 / dk'tronics
                               card or LambdaSpeak (SPEECH 0 / 1):
                               HELLO, TEST, CYBORG or numbers 0-63
  SIDTEST [ON]                 a chord on Speak&SID's SID (SID); ON
                               puts the board in its SID mode first
